2089 @VERSION@: a binary distribution for AIX

2089 is the game of 2048 in standard C89.  This is a binary distribution
for AIX on POWER and PowerPC, built with IBM's XL C on AIX 4.3.3.  It needs
only what AIX installs: the curses library, and X11 and Motif for the two X
programs.  The source is at https://github.com/nfinit/2089.

  bin/2089       the game on a terminal: full screen, or one line a move
  bin/x2089      the game in a window of its own, with Xlib only
  bin/xm2089     the game as a Motif application, with or without CDE
  man/man6/      their manual pages: 2089(6), x2089(6), xm2089(6)
  cde/           the CDE action, icons and help volume for xm2089

To install the programs and manual pages in /usr/local (as root):

  ./install.sh

and to put 2089 on the CDE desktop as well, in Application Manager's Games
group, with saved games that open from File Manager:

  ./install.sh -c

As another user, -c puts the CDE files in your own ~/.dt, and -p names
another place for the programs:

  ./install.sh -p $HOME -c

./install.sh -n shows what it would do: those are also the files to delete
to remove 2089.  Each program's -h lists its options.

AIX's man looks in /usr/share/man and /usr/dt/man only.  For the manual
pages, set MANPATH=/usr/local/man:/usr/share/man:/usr/dt/man (in
/etc/environment, or your .profile), or run man -M /usr/local/man 2089.

